# AGENTS.md

Notes for anyone changing {{title}}, people and coding agents alike.

{{title}} is an [eaglet](https://github.com/uniqtechteam/eaglet) app: modules, providers,
controllers and guards on top of Axum. Before writing eaglet code, read the reference
for coding agents: https://github.com/uniqtechteam/eaglet/blob/main/docs/llm-guide.md

## Commands

```bash
cargo run                                      # http://localhost:3000, API docs at /docs
cargo test
cargo fmt --check
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
eaglet g resource <name>                       # a CRUD feature, added to AppModule
```

## Layout

- `src/app_module.rs`: the root module. Every feature module is listed in its `imports`.
- `src/<feature>/`: one folder per feature. `mod.rs` holds the `#[module(...)]`, next to
  `controller.rs`, `service.rs`, `repository.rs` and `dto.rs`.
- `src/config.rs` and, with a database, `src/db.rs` (or `src/db/`): modules other features import.
- `tests/`: one file per feature, using `eaglet::testing::TestApp`.

## Rules

- Add features with `eaglet g`, or by hand in the same layout.
- Routes live in `#[controller]` impl blocks, and every controller and provider is listed in its
  module's `#[module(...)]`. Do not build an `axum::Router` by hand for them.
- Dependencies are `Arc<T>` fields of `#[injectable]` structs. State a provider owns is a field
  marked `#[inject(default)]`.
- Storage sits behind a trait bound with `provide!(dyn Trait => Impl)`, so tests can replace it with
  `override_provider`.
- Handlers and services return `Result<T, HttpError>`. Unexpected errors, such as a failed
  query, go through `HttpError::internal`, which logs them and tells the client nothing.
- Request bodies are `Valid<Json<T>>`, with `T` deriving `Deserialize`, `Validate` and `ToSchema`.
- Finish every change with `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo test`.
